Does the phone answer a search? (run on a laptop on the same network) <p><pre><code>import socket
s = socket.socket(socket.AF_INET, socket.SOCK_DGRAM)
s.bind(("LAPTOP_IP", 0)); s.settimeout(4)
s.sendto(b'M-SEARCH * HTTP/1.1\r\nHOST: 239.255.255.250:1900\r\n'
         b'MAN: "ssdp:discover"\r\nMX: 2\r\nST: ssdp:all\r\n\r\n',
         ("239.255.255.250", 1900))
try:
    while True: print(s.recvfrom(2048)[0].decode().splitlines()[:6])
except Exception as e: print("done", e)
</code></pre> Replies mentioning <code>HostLocal</code> or port 8200 mean the phone answers. Then check the app's SSDP packets by sender line to see that the laptop's search arrived.</p> <p>Other useful checks: <code>dns-sd -G v4 hostlocal.local</code> (mDNS), and the app's own SSDP counters (see DLNA diagnostics).</p>
